EXIT_CODES = """exit codes:
  0  done
  1  the device refused or the call failed
  2  bad usage, or no address recorded
  3  the device does not answer
  4  no such file or element
  5  the destination exists (pass --overwrite)
  6  the wait timed out
  7  the reference is stale: take a new snapshot
  8  the screen never settled, so no snapshot came back: try again
  9  a step found a screen it did not expect, and pressed nothing more
  10 doctor found a call this command relies on missing from the device
  11 read-only mode refused a command that changes the device
  12 the notes folder or a note on the screen is protected: pass --allow-notes
  13 the firmware was refused: not newer, not from Ratta, or the battery is too low
  14 the Ink Tools bridge app is not on the device: install its APK (apps/inktools-bridge)

a failure in --json has the fields: error, message, cause, next

each run adds one JSON line to ~/.cache/inkctl/history.jsonl, with the fields:
  time       when the run started, UTC
  command    the command's name, never its arguments
  seconds    how long the run took
  exit       its exit code
  error      the failure's name, or null
  app_before the app in front before the run
  app_after  the app in front after the run
  calls      each ADB call: call, seconds, exit (null when it timed out)
These fields are a public contract, like the exit codes.
The log never holds note content, screen text, file content or credentials.
The address is masked. A call keeps only its verb, unless --log-paths is passed.

https://github.com/martonpaulo/ink-tools
"""

